  "n": 185,
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "refId": "RV10-185:1",
      "text": "translated by"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "refId": "RV10-185:2",
      "text": "1. GREAT, unassailable must he the heavenly favour of' Three Gods,",
      "original": "महि त्रीणामवोऽस्तु द्युक्षं मित्रस्यार्यम्णः ।",
      "translit": "mahi trīṇāmavo'stu dyukṣaṃ mitrasyāryamṇaḥ |"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "refId": "RV10-185:3",
      "text": "Varuna, Mitra, Aryaman.",
      "original": "दुराधर्षं वरुणस्य",
      "translit": "durādharṣaṃ varuṇasya"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "refId": "RV10-185:4",
      "text": "2. O'er these, neither at home nor yet abroad or pathways that are Strange,",
      "original": "नहि तेषाममा चन नाध्वसु वारणेषु ।",
      "translit": "nahi teṣāmamā cana nādhvasu vāraṇeṣu |"
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "refId": "RV10-185:5",
      "text": "The evil-minded foe hath power",
      "original": "ईशे रिपुरघशंसः",
      "translit": "īśe ripuraghaśaṃsaḥ"
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "refId": "RV10-185:6",
      "text": "3. Nor over him, the man on whom the Sons of Aditi bestow Eternal light that he may live.",
      "original": "यस्मै पुत्रासो अदितेः प्र जीवसे मर्त्याय । ज्योतिर्यच्छन्त्यजस्रम्",
      "translit": "yasmai putrāso aditeḥ pra jīvase martyāya | jyotiryacchantyajasram"
    }
  ]
}
